/* Typed-state port of uha03_dec4.c - generated by tools/port_to_typed.py.
 *
 * The model state that lives outside the loaded image now sits in
 * typed struct members; the cells inside the image and the model
 * tables (addressed through computed arena offsets) still use the
 * arena.
 *
 * The file is maintained by hand on top of the generated version: the
 * per-block model pointers in the context are hand-written, and
 * re-running tools/port_to_typed.py would drop them.  See
 * DEC4_CLEAN_PLAN.md.
 */
/* UHARC 0.3 decompressor core 4 (methods 22..39) - portable C89 port.
 *
 * Ported from the uharc_u.lst disassembly + uharc_u.c decompile of the
 * UHARC 0.3 (uharc_u) decoder (control flow and constants come straight
 * from the listing; the decompile was hints only).
 *
 * Original -> port mapping (uharc_u.lst):
 *   sub_40BD9C (decode dispatch, methods 22..35) -> UhaDec4_03
 *   sub_415F6C (per-stream driver)     -> d3uc_decode_stream
 *   sub_413838 (startup: carve+memset) -> d3uc_startup (draft_a3.c)
 *   sub_415FD4 (match decode)          -> d3uc_decode_match (draft_m3.c)
 *   sub_41680C (fallback decoder)      -> d3uc_decode_fallback (draft_f3.c)
 *   sub_4164B8/416640/4177C0          -> d3uc_emit_literal/decode_length_sym/decode_offset_sym (draft_l3.c)
 *   sub_414290/414818 (top-ups)        -> d3uc_topup_dict_rebuild/topup_model_reinit (draft_t3.c)
 *   sub_423188/423140 (range coder)    -> d3uc_rc_decode/rc_update (draft_r3.c)
 *   sub_41E2B0/41E17C (stream input)   -> d3uc_get_byte/refill_input (draft_r3.c)
 *   sub_41E3BC/41E300 (stream output)  -> d3uc_put_byte/flush_out (here)
 *   sub_40D010 (progress callback)     -> d3uc_progress_callback (no-op stub here)
 *   sub_40C4B3 (bump carve)            -> d3u_carve (draft_a3.c, static)
 *   sub_40C9C0 (memset)                -> d3uc_fill (here)
 *
 * Memory model: the original carves ~21 blocks via sub_40C4B3 over the
 * pool cursor dword_436E48 and addresses everything (including DGROUP
 * globals) by absolute address. The port keeps one zeroed arena; every
 * original absolute address is used as an arena offset. Block pointers
 * (dword_4299B8..) are arena offsets handed out by the same carve order
 * and sizes as the original. The const slice uha03_dec4_dg.c (lifted
 * from uharc_u.exe) is copied 1:1 over 0x428000.. at init; BSS stays
 * calloc-zero.
 *
 * Register convention: x86 partial-register writes preserve the other
 * lanes, whose values the original inherits from caller leftovers. The C
 * port models each register as an unsigned variable, so every worker
 * auto is explicitly zero-initialised at declaration.
 */
